From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:56:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the lid angle sensor
 service

On 1.606 the J604 AOP firmware announces a las service: the AOP core
registers las.N.auto under the AOP, unbound. The J604 ADT has no las node
below /arm-io/aop/iop-aop-nub, so whether the service reports a hinge
angle on this machine is not known yet.

Enable the las child. aop_las (CONFIG_IIO_AOP_SENSOR_LAS=m in the official
configuration) only subscribes to the service's reports and sends nothing
to the AOP, so a service that never reports leaves an IIO angle channel
that reads ENODATA, and nothing else changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index a31895ac6b..9609db5a89 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -741,6 +741,15 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The J604 ADT has no las node under iop-aop-nub, but the AOP firmware
+ * announces a las service (las.N.auto on 1.606). Its driver only listens for
+ * reports, so the channel reads ENODATA if the service never sends one.
+ */
+&aop_las {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &aop_dart {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-4 */
 };
